<UserControl
    x:Class="FeWoLearning.Uno.Exercises.Beginner.Ex023_ThemeResource"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        TODO: Ex023 - declare theme dictionaries and consume them.

        On this UserControl's Resources, a ResourceDictionary with
        ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries holding two dictionaries, keyed "Light" and
        "Dark" - the keys are fixed names, not labels you choose. Each declares a
        SolidColorBrush keyed "CardBackground": White in Light, Black in Dark.

        The content: a Border named "Card", 40 by 20, whose Background is
        {ThemeResource CardBackground}.

        Use ThemeResource, not StaticResource. StaticResource would resolve once against
        whichever theme happened to be active and then never change again - which is the
        bug this exercise is about.
    -->

</UserControl>
